  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Signal, then fetch",
      "items": [
        "The database tells the app server about every change to watched job, order, customer, supplier and chat tables",
        "Job changes go out as a bare 'jobs changed' signal with no records; team chat events carry only the thread's newest-message preview and read marks",
        "Screens then re-read their own data through the normal, access-checked app APIs; the team bell updates its rows straight from the chat event"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why one relay",
      "items": [
        "Browsers have no database key, so they cannot listen to Supabase themselves",
        "The app server holds one shared Realtime channel and fans it out over Server-Sent Events",
        "Agent writes made straight in SQL are caught too, because the feed watches the database itself"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Safety nets",
      "items": [
        "Every screen re-syncs when its stream reconnects; data screens also re-read on tab focus, return or coming back online",
        "Slow fallback polling: team chat 10 s, portal chat 15 s, data screens and bells 60 s",
        "Supplier portal streams carry no ids or previews; the chat ping says only that the thread moved"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Supplier events wake Rosie",
      "items": [
        "Submitting availability or changing an order sends Rosie a notice on the thread of the job it belongs to (her main thread when there is no job)",
        "Saving answers without submitting is acknowledged but does not wake her",
        "Best-effort: if the harness is down the save still stands and only the wake-up is lost"
      ]
    }
  ]
